KG42.register("rules-072aa5d17e7a699d11671382",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R008","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R008","mechanism_id":"M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"Product differentiation may be implemented centrally for a dynamic and specific tax payment. Scope: Forward peer-to-peer MBED market; optional tax interpretation of bilateral trading costs. Condition: When product differentiation is implemented centrally as taxation.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["settlement.payment"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Forward peer-to-peer MBED market; optional tax interpretation of bilateral trading costs.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Product differentiation may be implemented centrally for a dynamic and specific tax payment. Scope: Forward peer-to-peer MBED market; optional tax interpretation of bilateral trading costs. Condition: When product differentiation is implemented centrally as taxation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"In a tax implementation of product differentiation, the perceived price corresponds to the price after tax, while trading prices correspond to the price before tax.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-e11"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"The P2P scheme attributes costs directly induced by the various trades and the agents involved, instead of socializing those costs as is most often done in a pool-based market framework.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e27"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":3,"printed_page":"996","section":"II-B. Product Differentiation","anchor_text":"nts expressed through be- cnm = cgnγgnm (7) are of g∈G The framework of product differentiation is g","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The framework of product differentiation is general and the meaning given to the bilateral trading costs depends in their interpretation. For instance product differentiation can be pushed centrally for a dynamic and specific tax payment or it can be used to better describe consumers' utility through the expression of their preferences. The former implementation may account for taxes, regulatory incentives and network charges, that will then influence the behaviour of market participants and eventual outcomes of the market... The latter implementation relies on the fact that there is a willingness to pay for certain characteristics of trades for instance for renewable sources of electricity [14], [15]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e27","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"problem at iteration k presented in (10) can be expressed as Llocn (pn, λkn, μn, μn) = Cn(pn) + Cn(p","equation_id":"(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With this definition, the first order optimality conditions of the relaxed problem, given by the KKT conditions, are for all agents n ∈ Ω and m ∈ ω_n a_n P_n + b_n + c_nm − λ_nm + μ̄_n − μ_n = 0 (15)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e28","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"problem at iteration k presented in (10) can be expressed as Llocn (pn, λkn, μn, μn) = Cn(pn) + Cn(p","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For any trade between two agents n and m, we define a new price, referred to as the perceived price, through λ̂_nm = λ_nm − c_nm (16) By opposition, the trading reciprocity constraint dual variables (λ_nm) are referred to as trading prices. As an example, in a tax implementation of product differentiation, the perceived price corresponds to the price after tax, while trading prices correspond to the price before tax."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e11","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-C. Primal Updates","anchor_text":"problem at iteration k presented in (10) can be expressed as Llocn (pn, λkn, μn, μn) = Cn(pn) + Cn(p","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For any trade between two agents n and m, we deﬁne a new price, referred to as the perceived price, through\nˆλnm = λnm −cnm                 (16)\nBy opposition, the trading reciprocity constraint dual variables (λnm) are referred to as trading prices. As an example, in a tax implementation of product differentiation, the perceived price corresponds to the price after tax, while trading prices correspond to the price before tax."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The frozen R008 V contains only settlement.payment, and neither the rule evidence v141-b-g01-e13 nor the additional same-mechanism passages define a decision variable whose domain is a settlement/payment choice for this rule. The source's decision variables P_nm, P_n, etc. are defined in other frozen rules (bidding/clearing) and are not declared in this rule's x; importing them would require explicit C.1 scope. This does not assert that the source lacks variables in the mechanism.","empty_theta_reason":"The R008 evidence does not define a tax rate, payment coefficient, or settlement parameter with a domain/value for this rule. The bilateral trading coefficient c_nm and criterion values are defined in the pricing/bidding rules; this rule's graph declares no theta objects, so they cannot be reused here without an explicit C.1 scope decision."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","quote":"For instance product differentiation can be pushed centrally for a dynamic and specific tax payment"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"b9a181b32f7daa323c09287e35d599613d339fb308ccd2ce7cbe7189fe8e5420","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen R008 has V=[settlement.payment], E=[], x=[], theta=[]. Its source anchor v141-b-g01-e13 is a qualitative interpretation: product differentiation may be implemented centrally as a dynamic/specific tax payment, or used to express consumer utility. No settlement/payment equation, tax rate function, payment amount, timing, or algorithmic payment rule is stated. The additional same-mechanism passages (v141-b-g01-e28/v141-b-g02-e11 on before/after-tax prices and v141-b-g01-e27 on direct cost attribution) are also qualitative. Therefore the current rule is a procedural/interpretive market-payment rule, not a formal mathematical settlement rule. B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is the core procedural constraint for R008; it attaches to the only frozen node in V, settlement.payment. No E edge exists in the frozen graph, and the source claim is an optional tax-payment interpretation rather than an edge-bearing formula."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The tax-implementation price terminology (perceived = after-tax price; trading price = before-tax price) is a supporting interpretation under the settlement.payment node; it introduces no new variable or parameter in this frozen rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The direct-cost attribution principle is a supporting settlement/payment design statement attached to settlement.payment; it is qualitative and introduces no new node or edge."}],"revision_requests":["If R008 is intended to capture a tax-payment or settlement-payment relation, C.1 should add source-backed nodes/edges connecting the product-differentiation/pricing objects to settlement.payment, with evidence showing the tax/payment flow. The frozen R008 currently has E=[].","C.1 should clarify whether settlement.payment is meant to represent the optional tax interpretation of bilateral trading costs or a distinct settlement mechanism; the supplied source passages are qualitative and do not provide a payment amount formula.","If a mathematical settlement rule is intended, C.1 must supply the relevant source equation (if any) and declare the corresponding x/theta variables and parameters with units and domains. No such equation appears in the R008 evidence.","B source_status remains unverified for the R008 evidence and the additional same-mechanism passages; if verified mathematical support is required, re-extraction or audit of the tax/settlement and cost-attribution passages is needed.","C.1 should resolve whether e27 (direct-cost attribution) and e28/e11 (before/after-tax price terminology) belong to the settlement.payment rule or to the pricing rule, since their catalog process_stage is pricing while their candidate_node_ids include settlement.payment."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
